## OVEN SPECIFICATIONS

<PIC:Manual24_4>
{{image description: Oven specifications table: power supply 120 VAC, 60 Hz; input power 1,500 W; cooking power 1,000 W, IEC 60705 standard; frequency 2,450 MHz; rated current 13 A; outer dimensions 29 15/16 in x 16 7/16 in x 15 5/8 in; cavity volume 1.8 cu. ft.; net weight 60 lbs.}}

### CONTROL SET-UP

You can change the default values for beep sound clock, display speed and defrost weight. (LBS/KG) See following chart for more information.<PIC:Manual24_9>
{{image description: Control set-up table with columns No., Function, No., and Result. Functions include sound on/off control, clock on/off control, scroll speed control with slow, normal, and fast speed, and LBS/KG choice control with Lbs. or Kg.}}

Example: To change defrost weight mode from Lbs to Kg.
<PIC:Manual24_10>
{{image description: Procedure and display table for changing defrost weight mode from Lbs to Kg. Steps show touching Control Set-Up, touching number 4, then number 2. Displays show SOUND ON/OFF TOUCH 1, CLOCK ON/OFF TOUCH 2, SCROLL SPEED TOUCH 3, LBS/KG CHOICE TOUCH 4; then LBS TOUCH 1 KG TOUCH 2; final display KG.}}

Example: To change defrost weight mode from Lbs to Kg.
<PIC:Manual24_10>
{{image description: Procedure and display table for changing defrost weight mode from Lbs to Kg. Steps show touching Control Set-Up, touching number 4, then number 2. Displays show SOUND ON/OFF TOUCH 1, CLOCK ON/OFF TOUCH 2, SCROLL SPEED TOUCH 3, LBS/KG CHOICE TOUCH 4; then LBS TOUCH 1 KG TOUCH 2; final display KG.}}

You can keep cooked food warm in your microwave oven for up to 99 minutes and 59 seconds. You can use Hold Warm by itself or to follow a cooking cycle automatically.


Example: To use Hold Warm.

<PIC:Manual24_14>
{{image description: Procedure and display table for Hold Warm. Steps show touching Hold Warm pad and Start pad. Displays read HOLD WARM TOUCH START and WARM.}}

<PIC:Manual24_15>
{{image description: Small table listing food type and recommended quantity for Hold Warm: Liquid 1-2 cups, Dry 5-10 ozs.}}

Example: To recall the custom recipe
<PIC:Manual24_17>
{{image description: Procedure and display table for Favorite Recipe. Steps show touching Favorite Recipe and touching Start. Display shows 2:00 TOUCH START OR POWER, then time counting down.}}

Example: To cook food for 8 minutes, 30 seconds at  100%  power.
<PIC:Manual24_18>
{{image description: Procedure and display table for timed cooking. Steps show entering cook time 8 3 0 and touching Start. Displays read 8:30 TOUCH START OR POWER, then time counting down, power 100.}}

POPCORN lets you pop 3.0 and 3.5 ounce bags of commercially packaged microwave popcorn. Pop only one package at a time. If you are using a microwave popcorn popper, follow manufacturer's instructions.

Example: To pop popcorn.<PIC:Manual24_23>
{{image description: Procedure and display table for Popcorn. Step 1 says touch Popcorn pad; display shows POPCORN, then an arrow to SENSING.}}

POTATO lets you bake one or several potatoes without selecting cooking times and power levels.

Example: To cook 2 potatoes.<PIC:Manual24_25>
{{image description: Procedure and display table for Potato. Step 1 says touch Potato pad; display shows POTATO, then an arrow to SENSING.}}

VEGETABLE has preset cook powers for 3 food categories: Fresh, Frozen and Canned.

Example: To cook frozen vegetables<PIC:Manual24_26>
{{image description: Procedure and display table for Vegetable. Steps show touching Vegetable, choosing food category by touching number 2 for Frozen Vegetable, then sensing. Displays list FRESH TOUCH 1, FROZEN TOUCH 2, CANNED TOUCH 3; then FROZEN VEGETABLE and SENSING.}}

COOK lets you heat common microwave-prepared foods without needing to program times and Power Levels. COOK has preset power for 3 food categories: Frozen Entree, Casserole and Rice.

Example: To cook rice.<PIC:Manual24_27>
{{image description: Procedure and display table for sensor Cook with category Rice. Steps show touching Cook and choosing food category number 3. Displays show SELECT MENU 1 TO 3, RICE, and SENSING. A category table lists Frozen Entree 1, Casserole 2, Rice 3.}}

- When the cook time is over, you will hear four beeps and END will display.
- Recommended amounts:<PIC:Manual24_28>
{{image description: Quantity table for Cook categories: Frozen Entree 10-21 ozs., Casserole 1-4 cups, Rice 1/2-2 cups.}}

### REHEAT(SENSOR)

Reheat lets you heat foods without needing to program times and Power Levels. Reheat has preset Power Levels for 3 categories: Casserole, Dinner Plate and Soup/Sauce
<PIC:Manual24_29>
{{image description: Category table for Reheat touch pad numbers: Casserole 1, Dinner Plate 2, Soup/Sauce 3.}}

Example: To reheat Casserole
<PIC:Manual24_30>
{{image description: Procedure and display table for sensor Reheat. Steps show touching Reheat and choosing Casserole with number 1. Displays show SELECT MENU 1 TO 3, CASSEROLE, and SENSING.}}


- When the cook time is over, you will hear four beeps and END will display.
- Recommended amounts:<PIC:Manual24_31>
{{image description: Quantity table for Reheat categories: Casserole 1-4 cups, Dinner Plate 1-2 servings, Soup/Sauce 1-4 cups.}}

