- Recommended amounts:<PIC:Manual24_31>
{{image description: Quantity table for Reheat categories: Casserole 1-4 cups, Dinner Plate 1-2 servings, Soup/Sauce 1-4 cups.}}

Your microwave oven is preset with three defrost sequences. Using AUTO DEFROST is the best way to defrost frozen foods. The Auto Defrost Chart on pages 19-20 provides some basic guidelines for using the three defrost sequences.

<PIC:Manual24_32>
{{image description: Auto Defrost category table listing Meat touch pad 1, Poultry touch pad 2, and Fish touch pad 3.}}

Example: To defrost 1.2 lbs. of ground beef.

<PIC:Manual24_33>
{{image description: Procedure and display table for Auto Defrost. Steps show touching Auto Defrost, choosing Meat with number 1, entering weight with 1 and 2, and touching Start. Displays include MEAT TOUCH 1 POULTRY TOUCH 2 FISH TOUCH 3, ENTER WEIGHT, 1.2 LBS TOUCH START, and time counting down and DEFROST.}}

### WEIGHT CONVERSION CHART


To enter food weight in Auto Defrost, you must specify pounds and tenths of a pound. If the weight on the food package is in fractions of a pound, you can use the following chart to convert the weight to decimals<PIC:Manual24_34>
{{image description: Weight conversion chart with equivalent ounce weight and pounds. It maps 1.6 to .10, 3.2 to .20, 4.0 to .25 one-quarter pounds, 4.8 to .30, 6.4 to .40, 8.0 to .50 one-half pounds, 9.6 to .60, 11.2 to .70, 12.0 to .75 three-quarter pounds, 12.8 to .80, 14.4 to .90, and 16.0 to 1.00 one pound.}}

#### Poultry Setting

<PIC:Manual24_36>
{{image description: Auto Defrost chart for poultry. Chicken whole up to 6 lbs should be turned over, warm areas covered with aluminum foil, placed breast-side up on a microwavable roast rack, and finished in cold water. Cut-up chicken is separated and rearranged. Cornish hens and turkey breast under 6 lbs are turned over and finished with cold water.}}

#### FISH AND SHELLFISH COOKING TABLE

<PIC:Manual24_42>
{{image description: Fish cooking chart with columns Fish, Power Level, Cooking Time, and Directions. Rows include fish fillets, fish steaks, whole fish, scallops, and shelled shrimp, with power levels HI or 7 and cooking times such as 3 1/2 to 6 minutes; directions mention arranging in a single layer, covering with vented plastic wrap, and letting stand.}}

#### MEAT COOKING TABLE

<PIC:Manual24_43>
{{image description: Meat cooking chart with columns Meat, Power Level, Cooking Time, and Directions. It includes beef hamburgers, sirloin tip roast, lamb roast, bacon slices, pork chops, loin roast, and sausage links, with power levels HI, 5, or 3 and temperatures such as 135 degrees F, 145 degrees F, 155 degrees F, 165 degrees F, and 170 degrees F.}}

#### POULTRY COOKING TABLE

<PIC:Manual24_44>
{{image description: Poultry cooking chart with columns Poultry, Power Level, Cooking Time, and Directions. Rows include chicken pieces, whole chicken, and whole Cornish hens at power level HI, with minutes per pound and instructions to wash, place in a dish or rack, cover with waxed paper, turn or shield parts, and let stand covered with foil.}}

#### PASTA COOKING TABLE

<PIC:Manual24_45>
{{image description: Pasta cooking chart with columns Pasta, Power Level, Cooking Time, and Directions. Rows include spaghetti, macaroni, lasagna noodles, and egg noodles, with water amounts, power levels HI and 5, cooking times, and directions to combine water and salt, cover or vent, stir, and drain.}}

#### RICE COOKING TABLE

<PIC:Manual24_46>
{{image description: Rice cooking chart with columns Rice, Power Level, Cooking Time, and Directions. Rows include long grain, brown, long grain and wild rice mix, and quick cooking rice, with water amounts, power levels HI and 5, cooking times, and directions to combine hot water and salt, stir, cover, and let stand.}}

2. Wash in dishwasher or soak grease filter in hot water and a mild detergent. Rinse well and shake to dry. Do not use ammonia or place in a dishwasher. The aluminum filter will darken.
<PIC:Manual24_47>
{{image description: Underside line drawing of an over-the-range microwave with an arrow pointing to the bottom filter or vent area.}}

3. To reinstall the filter, slide it into the side slot, then push up and toward oven center to lock
<PIC:Manual24_48>
{{image description: Line drawing of hands washing a mesh grease filter under running water at a sink.}}


<PIC:Manual24_49>
{{image description: Underside drawing of the microwave with a bold arrow indicating the bottom filter or vent panel being pulled or slid out.}}

4. Remove old filter.
<PIC:Manual24_50>
{{image description: Installation/removal drawing of a microwave being held from both sides under a cabinet, with two screws shown above the top mounting area.}}

5. Slide a new charcoal filter into place. The filter should rest at the angle shown.
<PIC:Manual24_51>
{{image description: Front view of a microwave with the grille or vent opened. A hand pulls a mesh filter or charcoal filter outward, indicated by a bold arrow.}}

6. Slide the bottom of the grill into place. Push the top until it snaps into place. Replace the mounting screws. Turn the power back on at the main power supply and set the clock.
<PIC:Manual24_52>
{{image description: Front microwave view showing a large rectangular mesh filter installed behind the top grille above the door.}}

5. Turn the power back on at the main power supply or plug in the oven.
<PIC:Manual24_53>
{{image description: Underside close-up of the microwave showing the bottom light covers, central vent/filter area, and a small screw or latch in the middle.}}

4. Remove bulb holder
<PIC:Manual24_54>
{{image description: Drawing of a microwave being supported from both sides under a cabinet, with two top mounting screws shown above.}}

5. Lift up the bulb holder
<PIC:Manual24_55>
{{image description: Front top grille area of the microwave with a bold arrow pointing to a small rectangular light or filter housing behind the grille.}}

8. Slide the bottom of the vent cover into place. Push the top until it snaps into place. Replace the mounting screws. Turn the power back on at the main power supply or plug in the oven.
